In triangle $ABC$, $\angle BAC = 30^\circ$, $AC = 6$ units, and $\angle ACB = 90^\circ$. If $D$ is a point on $AC$ such that $AD = x$ units, and $E$ is a point on $AB$ such that $AE = y$ units, find the area of triangle $ADE$ in terms of $x$ and $y$. 

[asy]
unitsize(1inch);
pair P,Q,R,D,E;
P = (0,0);
Q= (sqrt(3),0);
R = (0,1);
D = (x/6)*R;
E = (y/2)*Q;
draw (P--Q--R--P,linewidth(0.9));
draw(D--E,linewidth(0.9));
draw(rightanglemark(Q,P,R,3));
label("$A$",P,S);
label("$B$",Q,S);
label("$C$",R,N);
label("$D$",D,W);
label("$E$",E,S);
label("$6$",R/2,W);
label("$30^\circ$",(1.25,0),N);
label("$x$",D/2,W);
label("$y$",(E+P)/2,S);
[/asy]

